```rust
struct Line {
    start: Point,
    end: Point,
    length: f64, // derivable from start and end, stored redundantly
}

impl Line {
    fn set_start(&mut self, new_start: Point) {
        self.start = new_start;
        // If the developer forgets to recalculate self.length here, an invariant breaks.
    }
}
```

fix:
Remove unnecessary derived storage and expose an on-demand calculation method. If expensive caching is justified, keep it behind the same encapsulation boundary as all relevant mutations and maintain its coherence rather than requiring callers to update both representations.
```rust
struct Line {
    start: Point,
    end: Point,
}

impl Line {
    fn length(&self) -> f64 {
        self.start.distance_to(&self.end)
    }
}
```
